# libei -- emulated input, and the reason it is packaged BEFORE xwayland rather
# than alongside it.
#
# This is the library X11 clients' synthetic input travels through under a
# Wayland compositor: XTEST, and therefore the input half of remote desktop.
# Xwayland links it, and the interesting part is what happens when it is
# missing -- which is nothing at all. See the ordering note below.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
#
# md5 1bed8a57a52c3ff38baa90c57661dbbf is the book's, checked against the same
# bytes as the sha256 below.
SRC_URL=https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libinput/libei/-/archive/1.4.1/libei-1.4.1.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=1d6549c2520e67502fb829987bbf56a2dcf7d1a17ebe90c3ad652df06cdb08f9
SRC_DIR=libei-1.4.1

# -Dsd-bus-provider=libelogind IS THE ONE FLAG HERE THAT CHANGES WHAT GETS
# BUILT, and it is the same trap pipewire handles with -Dlogind-provider.
#
# The option defaults to 'auto', and 'auto' is not a search for the best
# provider -- it is a FIRST MATCH over a fixed list, in this order
# (meson.build:87):
#
#     providers = ['libsystemd', 'libelogind', 'basu']
#
# Duct's elogind installs a libsystemd.pc compatibility symlink, so
# dependency('libsystemd') SUCCEEDS on the first iteration and the loop never
# reaches libelogind. The result is not a build failure, it is a build that sets
#
#     config_h.set10('HAVE_LIBSYSTEMD', ... dep_sdbus.name() == 'libsystemd')
#     config_h.set10('HAVE_LIBELOGIND', ... dep_sdbus.name() == 'libelogind')
#
# with the first true and the second false, on a system that has no systemd --
# so the source compiles its systemd branch against elogind's alias. Naming the
# provider is what makes the two macros describe reality.
#
# -Dliboeffis=enabled IS REQUIRED BY XWAYLAND AND NOT MERELY NICE. Xwayland's
# meson takes liboeffis-1.0 when xwayland_ei is 'portal', which is how X11
# clients reach input through the RemoteDesktop portal rather than a bare
# socket. It is stated rather than left at 'auto' because 'auto' here resolves
# through the sd-bus provider above -- so its value would be decided by the same
# accident this recipe just closed.
#
# -Dlibei and -Dlibeis are both stated for the same reason every pipewire option
# is: they default to 'auto', and an auto feature produces a different artefact
# in a different image without saying so. libeis is the SERVER side -- the
# compositor's half -- and while nothing in this tree links it yet, shipping the
# library is what makes the package's name true.
#
# -Dtests=disabled: the test suite needs pytest, structlog, strenum and
# dbusmock, none of which are packaged, and munit, which is a subproject wrap.
# BLFS disables it too.
#
# -Ddocumentation IS DELIBERATELY NOT PASSED. It is an array option whose
# default is already the empty list, and passing an array literal on a meson
# command line is a syntax hazard for a value that would change nothing.
MESON_ARGS="-Dsd-bus-provider=libelogind \
-Dlibei=enabled -Dlibeis=enabled -Dliboeffis=enabled \
-Dtests=disabled"
